Original change's description:
> [SimpleCache] Prevent doomed entries from mutating SimpleIndex
>
> This CL guards SimpleEntryImpl index mutations so an already-doomed
> entry cannot remove or overwrite a replacement entry sharing the same
> hash in SimpleIndex.
>
> Previously, if a doomed SimpleEntryImpl remained open after another
> entry was created for the same key, an I/O or checksum failure on the
> doomed entry removed the replacement entry's hash from SimpleIndex.
> That caused subsequent OpenEntry calls to miss the live entry even
> though its files remained on disk (so CacheStorage delete missed it and
> OpenOrCreateEntry later reopened it). In-memory metadata and trailer
> prefetch updates on a doomed entry could also clobber the active
> entry's performance hints.
>
> This fixes the SimpleCache trigger used in b/583238770; the main
> CacheStorage stream-truncation fix is in crrev.com/c/8835441.
>
